{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-stable-atom-decidable","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:stable-atom-decidable","kind":"proposition","title":"Stability is decidable for any (Z, N) at fixed q","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-stable-atom"],"tags":["decidability","stability","ilp","atom"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.StableAtom.decidable","text":"stable-atom-decidable.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/stable-atom-decidable.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:stable-atom-decidable\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> be an atom-knot of type <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(Z, N)</code> and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> be a substrate parameter in the generic locus. <a href=\"#def:stable-atom\">Stability of the atom</a> at fixed <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> is <strong>decidable</strong>. There exists an algorithm that returns <code>True</code> if <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> is stable at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> and <code>False</code> otherwise.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/stable-atom-decidable.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"9.10.10"}
